theorem one-more
  note        An "if and only if" proved a direction at a time.
  let n ∈ ℤ                                                           (H1)
  then n + 1 = 3 ↔ n = 2

1.  n + 1 = 3 ↔ n = 2
    both directions

    direction
    assume n + 1 = 3                                                  (D1)

    1.1.  n = 2
          algebra, from D1

    direction
    assume n = 2                                                      (D2)

    1.2.  n + 1 = 3
          algebra, from D2
